<section class="cs-what">
  <div class="fi">
    <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">The Object</div>
    <p class="csw-statement">Nothing else<br>like it <em>exists.</em></p>
    <p class="csw-body">A hand-knitted mohair cardigan, button band reinforced to carry the weight of stone. Five to seven natural stone buttons. One story card per stone, on archival paper, in the package. An archive number on the label. This is not a metaphor. Every stone is real. Every origin is documented. Every story is true.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="csw-cards fi d2">
    <div class="csw-card"><div class="csw-card-label">The Garment</div><div class="csw-card-title">Hand-knitted Ankara Mohair</div><p class="csw-card-body">Open lace pattern. Reinforced ribbed button band to carry the weight of stone buttons. Made in Istanbul. Wearable for years, not seasons.</p></div>
    <div class="csw-card"><div class="csw-card-label">The Buttons</div><div class="csw-card-title">5&#8211;7 Natural Stones</div><p class="csw-card-body">Collected from Turkish coastlines, Aegean beaches, Anatolian forests and beyond. Each stone is assessed, drilled with a diamond-tipped water-cooled press, and set with a reinforced shank.</p></div>
    <div class="csw-card"><div class="csw-card-label">The Record</div><div class="csw-card-title">Story Cards &#183; Archival Paper</div><p class="csw-card-body">One card per stone. The origin &#8212; where it was found, what the place was. Written by LIYreal from direct knowledge of the collection.</p></div>
    <div class="csw-card"><div class="csw-card-label">The Number</div><div class="csw-card-title">Archive Edition &#183; Numbered</div><p class="csw-card-body">Cloud &amp; Stone No. 001 through No. 008 at proof drop. Drop-based, closed when sold. Never an evergreen product.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="section-rule"><span>The Stones</span></div>
<section class="stones-section">
  <div class="ss-head fi"><h2 class="ss-title">Eight <em>stones.</em><br>Eight origins.</h2><div class="ss-count">Proof Drop &#183; No. 001&#8211;008</div></div>
  <div class="stones-grid fi d1">
    <div class="stone-card"><div class="sc-num">Button &#183; 01 &#183; No. 001</div><div class="sc-pebble sc-p1"></div><div class="sc-origin">Aegean Coast &#183; Turkey</div><div class="sc-place">Pale sea agate</div><p class="sc-story">Found at the waterline near Bodrum, early morning. The stone had been worn smooth by forty years of tide. Its colour is the colour of winter sky over the Aegean.</p><div class="sc-footer"><span class="sc-wm">LIYreal</span><span class="sc-log">Logged</span></div></div>
    <div class="stone-card"><div class="sc-num">Button &#183; 02 &#183; No. 001</div><div class="sc-pebble sc-p2"></div><div class="sc-origin">Anatolian Plateau &#183; Turkey</div><div class="sc-place">River obsidian</div><p class="sc-story">From the bed of a stream above Nev&#351;ehir. Black and still as the plateau in winter. The region has been volcanic for ten million years.</p><div class="sc-footer"><span class="sc-wm">LIYreal</span><span class="sc-log">Logged</span></div></div>
    <div class="stone-card"><div class="sc-num">Button &#183; 03 &#183; No. 002</div><div class="sc-pebble sc-p3"></div><div class="sc-origin">Black Sea Shore &#183; Turkey</div><div class="sc-place">Dark sea basalt</div><p class="sc-story">The Black Sea coast gives different stones than the Aegean. Heavier, darker, more formal. Found at dusk, the water still moving across the rock shelf.</p><div class="sc-footer"><span class="sc-wm">LIYreal</span><span class="sc-log">Logged</span></div></div>
    <div class="stone-card"><div class="sc-num">Button &#183; 04 &#183; No. 003</div><div class="sc-pebble sc-p4"></div><div class="sc-origin">Bosphorus &#183; Istanbul</div><div class="sc-place">Warm limestone</div><p class="sc-story">From the European shore near Rumeli. Istanbul is on both sides of a strait between two seas. The stone carries that position &#8212; warm, transitional, between.</p><div class="sc-footer"><span class="sc-wm">LIYreal</span><span class="sc-log">Logged</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:4rem"><button class="btn btn-outline" onclick="go('first')">Reserve Cloud &amp; Stone No. 001&#8211;008 <span class="arr">&#8594;</span></button></div>
</section>
<section class="cs-map-section" id="csMapSec">
  <div class="csm-header fi">
    <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:2rem">The Map</div>
    <h2 class="csm-title">The Constellation<br><em>Map</em></h2>
    <p class="csm-body">Every stone in the Cloud &amp; Stone archive is logged: origin region, story, archive number, and current location as reported by the wearer. The map is a living record. It moves as the pieces travel.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="map-box fi d1">
